+Runtime and Source Prerequisites
+--------------------------------
+
+Use a checkout that matches this documentation. Container images can contain an
+older checkout: clone or mount the required source revision and run commands from
+its repository root. Initialize recipe examples with
+``git submodule update --init --recursive``.
+
+Install the driver and firmware on the host. Containers must expose the required
+NPU devices and driver libraries; install or mount a compatible CANN runtime
+inside the container. Source the installed CANN ``set_env.sh`` in every shell
+before starting Python or Ray, adjusting the installation path if necessary:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   source /usr/local/Ascend/ascend-toolkit/set_env.sh
+   npu-smi info
+   # After installing the matching torch / torch_npu pair:
+   python -c "import torch, torch_npu; print(torch.__version__, torch_npu.__version__); assert torch.npu.is_available()"
+
+Missing ``libhccl.so`` means the CANN libraries or their environment are missing.
+An undefined symbol in ``libtorch_npu.so`` can indicate mismatched torch and
+torch_npu builds. Fix the installation before training; disabling backend autoload
+does not make NPU execution work. Use separate environments for the vLLM and
+SGLang combinations below.
+
+The version tables describe source refs and target dependencies, not an inventory
+of an arbitrary existing container. In particular, ``26.2.0_*`` entries for the
+Ascend adapters are Git branches/tags, not necessarily the versions printed by
+``pip show``. Verify the source ref with ``git -C <component-dir> describe --always --tags``
+and ``git -C <component-dir> rev-parse HEAD`` as well as the installed package version.
+
+The yum commands below target openEuler/RHEL-like hosts. On Ubuntu, use the CANN
+installer and prerequisites for Ubuntu from the official download page; do not
+run yum or install a host driver inside an application container. Install the
+Python version in the selected backend's table separately from the system Python.
+
+For restricted networks, download the selected source revision (including Git
+submodules), wheels and datasets on a connected machine and transfer them to the
+same environment that will run the commands. Existing local checkouts can be
+reused after checking their revision. Configure your proxy and trusted CA bundle
+for Git/pip if required; certificate errors should be fixed by correcting the
+system clock and CA configuration.
+
