+Runtime, Build and Network Prerequisites
+----------------------------------------
+
+The tables below describe the target source-build combination, not packages
+preinstalled in every container. Use a checkout matching this guide. Read the
+`general runtime prerequisites <install_guidance.rst>`_ for driver/CANN mounts,
+torch/torch_npu version checks, Git refs versus distribution versions, and
+restricted-network setup. ``triton-ascend`` and ``triton_ascend`` are normalized
+spellings of the same distribution name. Similarly, a Git tag ``v0.5.0`` may
+produce a package version such as ``0.5.0+<commit>``. TransformerEngineNPU is
+imported as ``transformer_engine``; query that distribution and its source ref.
+
+Use a separate Python 3.12 environment rather than replacing the host's system
+Python. Install `uv <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/>`_
+first if it is not available, then prepare a common parent for source checkouts:
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   export INSTALL_ROOT="${INSTALL_ROOT:-${HOME}/verl-950-build}"
+   mkdir -p "$INSTALL_ROOT"
+   cd "$INSTALL_ROOT"
+   uv venv --python 3.12 --seed .venv
+   source .venv/bin/activate
+   python --version
+   pip install "cmake>=3.26" ninja wheel pybind11 packaging "setuptools>=64" setuptools-scm
+
+Compile inside an environment with a C/C++ compiler, make, Python development
+headers and CANN development tools for the installed hardware. On Ubuntu the
+host/container build prerequisites include ``build-essential`` and
+``python3-dev``; on openEuler use the matching ``gcc``, ``gcc-c++``, ``make`` and
+Python development packages. Kernel headers are host-driver prerequisites, not a
+way to install the required Python version. NPU kernels use CANN/AscendC; a CUDA
+toolkit is not the prerequisite for these NPU builds. Download Git submodules
+before compiling. ``--no-build-isolation`` reuses the active environment's build
+packages, and ``--no-deps`` requires dependencies to be installed beforehand.
+Build time depends on CPU resources and cache state; consult the first compiler
+error rather than treating every failure as a missing package.
+
+For GitCode/GitHub restrictions, transfer the selected source refs (including
+submodules) from a connected machine. For unavailable package indexes, prepare a
+wheelhouse for the same Python, architecture and CANN stack, then install with
+``pip install --no-index --find-links=/path/to/wheelhouse <package>``. Fix DNS,
+proxy/CA settings and system time for TLS errors, including redirects to a
+second hostname. Use ``PIP_CERT`` or your organization's trusted CA bundle when
+required; do not bypass certificate validation to work around a wrong clock.
+
